---
import Breadcrumb from "@/components/astro/Breadcrumb.astro";
import styles from "@/style/page/content.module.css";
import rosterAudit from "@/data/research/roster-audit.json";
import skillAudit from "@/data/research/skill-audit.json";
import currentProfileKits from "@/data/research/current-profile-kits.json";
const unmatchedReference = rosterAudit.unmatchedReference as Array<{ slug: string; url: string }>;
const unmatchedLocal = rosterAudit.unmatchedLocal as Array<{ slug: string; name: string }>;
const pagePrinciples = [
  { label: "Game fields", title: "Profiles stay close to the game", body: "Profiles focus on elements, roles, skills, traits, forms, habitats and evolution paths. When a field is not clear enough to show, it is left blank instead of guessed.", items: ["Creature profiles", "Skill and trait links", "Forms and evolution paths"] },
  { label: "Player guidance", title: "Guides explain a choice, not a script", body: "Guides and team templates are written as starting points for a real player decision. They show the trade-off, then leave room for your own roster and activity.", items: ["Guides", "Team templates", "Route planning"] },
  { label: "Ongoing review", title: "A page can be updated without pretending it is final", body: "Updates are dated, rankings are labeled for what they measure, and unclear connections are kept out until they can be matched with confidence.", items: ["Update timeline", "Player vote results", "Correction requests"] },
];


---
<>
    <section class={styles.compactHero}><div class="container"><Breadcrumb items={[{ label: "How this site works" }]} /><span class={styles.kicker}>Clear labels, fewer guesses</span><h1>How Aniimo Keeps Pages Useful</h1><p>Game fields, player-made tools and incomplete connections are handled differently, so you can tell what a page is actually helping you decide.</p></div></section>
    <section class={styles.contentSection}><div class="container"><div class={styles.sourceDirectory}>{pagePrinciples.map((principle) => <article><span class={styles.status}>{principle.label}</span><h2>{principle.title}</h2><p>{principle.body}</p><ul>{principle.items.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul></article>)}</div><section class="rosterAudit"><h2>Roster coverage review</h2><p>The current index combines {rosterAudit.officialSnapshotCount - 1} species entries from an older official wiki snapshot with {rosterAudit.supplementCount} community launch records. Witchin uses the current name Hexxin; Fennelun remains accessible as a legacy page and appears as Lunara’s temporary form. The <a href={rosterAudit.sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">community Aniilog directory</a> listed {rosterAudit.referenceCount} species on {rosterAudit.checkedAt}; our current index has {rosterAudit.localCount}.</p>{(rosterAudit.unmatchedReference.length > 0 || rosterAudit.unmatchedLocal.length > 0) ? <div><section><h3>Listed there, unmatched here</h3><ul>{unmatchedReference.map((record) => <li><a href={record.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{record.slug}</a></li>)}</ul></section><section><h3>Indexed here, unmatched there</h3><ul>{unmatchedLocal.map((record) => <li>{record.name}</li>)}</ul></section></div> : <p>All current reference species slugs are matched. Older wiki fields remain available where clearly labeled as historical.</p>}<p>Current skills, form portraits and seven-field base blocks cover {currentProfileKits.profiles.length} Aniimo and {currentProfileKits.profiles.reduce((sum, profile) => sum + profile.forms.length, 0)} forms (reviewed {currentProfileKits.reviewedAt}). The {skillAudit.checkedAt} audit found {skillAudit.changedCount} differences in current skill names, descriptions, costs, power, form unlock links, form labels or seven-field base blocks against those reference pages. The older wiki snapshot still differs on {skillAudit.legacySnapshotChangedCount} profiles; those skill records are superseded on the live pages.</p><p>AniimoVerse is a community source. Its launch data is shown with a direct source link on each profile; historical wiki fields and player guidance use separate labels.</p></section><div class={styles.seoCopy}><div><span class={styles.kicker}>Our editorial rule</span><h2>Do not turn a gap into a claim</h2><p>Game fields stay separate from player suggestions. If information conflicts, belongs to an older test build or cannot be matched to a current profile, the page states less rather than pretending to know more.</p></div><aside><h2>What you will see</h2><p><strong>Game fields</strong> for profiles and relationships</p><p><strong>Player guidance</strong> for guides and team templates</p><p><strong>Clear limits</strong> when information is incomplete</p></aside></div></div></section>
  </>
<style>.rosterAudit{margin-top:24px;padding:24px;border:1px solid #d7e4eb;border-radius:18px;background:#f5faff}.rosterAudit h2{margin:0 0 8px}.rosterAudit p{max-width:85ch;color:#526b80;line-height:1.6}.rosterAudit>div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px}.rosterAudit h3{font-size:17px}.rosterAudit ul{margin:0;padding-left:20px;line-height:1.8}.rosterAudit a{color:#246fc6}@media(max-width:700px){.rosterAudit>div{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
